The elements of the system of finitely generated subsystems are order-isomorphic to the subsystems of D. The forward map reconstructs a subsystem from a filter, and the inverse induces a filter from a subsystem. The two round trips are the identities already established for those maps. Order is preserved and reflected because subsystemhood of the reconstructed systems is inclusion of their neighbourhoods, and confirmation of a generated neighbourhood is generator-wise membership in the reconstructed subsystem.
